<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador net reserves up to $2.07 billion at May 3.</title>
<headline>Ecuador net reserves up to $2.07 billion at May 3.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday its net international reserves stood at $2.07 billion on May 3, up $22 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In April 1997, international reserves grew $128 million.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of 1996, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
